# CODEOWNERS: every path has a primary owner and a named secondary reviewer (spec §4.2; C15).
#
# On each line the FIRST handle is the primary owner and the SECOND is the secondary reviewer.
# GitHub requests review from every listed owner, and with "Require review from Code Owners"
# enabled on main, a PR needs approval from one of them who is not its author, which in
# practice is the secondary reviewer. Later lines override earlier ones for the same path.
#
# HOW TO REPLACE THE PLACEHOLDERS (Week 2, when TEAM_CONTRACT.md is signed):
#   Option A (recommended): create five GitHub teams in the organisation, named r1-kernel,
#     r2-vfs-db, r3-wm-ui, r4-ai and r5-qa-devops, each with one member, and replace
#     "plotinium-org" below with the organisation name.
#   Option B: replace each team handle with the member's GitHub username, for example
#     "@plotinium-org/r1-kernel" -> "@ali-khan".
# Until then GitHub shows these owners as unknown; nothing else breaks.
#
#   R1 Kernel / Systems Architect         @plotinium-org/r1-kernel
#   R2 VFS / Database Engineer            @plotinium-org/r2-vfs-db
#   R3 WM / UI Subsystem Lead             @plotinium-org/r3-wm-ui
#   R4 AI Pipeline Specialist             @plotinium-org/r4-ai
#   R5 QA / DevOps & Integration Engineer @plotinium-org/r5-qa-devops

# Fallback for anything not listed below
